WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:49.884
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:50.154 --> 00:53.324
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

3
01:03.793 --> 01:06.045
SHIPPING COST

4
01:24.897 --> 01:25.898
Good morning.

5
01:33.364 --> 01:35.908
- Hello, Mr. Gong. - Morning, Ms. Jang.

6
01:45.334 --> 01:46.585
When did you get to work?

7
01:47.294 --> 01:49.255
I got to the café an hour ago.

8
01:50.506 --> 01:52.466
I came in an hour and ten minutes ago.

9
01:53.718 --> 01:55.010
Why did you come so early?

10
01:55.094 --> 01:56.095
What about you?

11
01:56.178 --> 01:57.471
I asked you first.

12
01:57.722 --> 01:59.432
I don't want to answer first.

13
01:59.515 --> 02:01.142
That's why I asked you first.

14
02:04.228 --> 02:05.604
I do this when I'm nervous.

15
02:07.356 --> 02:08.524
I work harder

16
02:09.150 --> 02:10.693
get things ready faster

17
02:10.776 --> 02:12.528
try to sleep less

18
02:13.112 --> 02:15.156
and even run simulations in my head.

19
02:18.075 --> 02:19.243
It's your turn now.

20
02:21.996 --> 02:23.456
I miscalculated the time.

21
02:24.749 --> 02:28.210
I meant to get here a little early, but I came too early.

22
02:31.881 --> 02:34.967
Aren't I pathetic, how I'm always tense and nervous?

23
02:36.385 --> 02:37.386
Not at all.

24
02:37.845 --> 02:40.306
I think that's why you're good at what you do.

25
02:40.806 --> 02:42.016
You don't make mistakes.

26
02:42.433 --> 02:44.852
Me? I make a ton of mistakes.

27
02:45.269 --> 02:46.270
Do you?

28
02:47.021 --> 02:49.231
Nothing ever goes the way I plan.

29
02:49.732 --> 02:50.983
I make loads of mistakes.

30
02:52.777 --> 02:54.069
But if you practice hard enough

31
02:55.362 --> 02:57.114
you can make up for the mistakes.

32
03:00.034 --> 03:02.036
Let's go. Time to make some mistakes.

33
03:15.716 --> 03:20.262
EPISODE 7: NOTHING HAS CHANGED

34
03:22.181 --> 03:23.390
SALES DIVISION 2 EXPORT SALES CONTRACT

35
03:31.607 --> 03:32.691
Mr. Choi.

36
03:33.901 --> 03:37.071
I asked for all documents produced or received by Sales Division 2

37
03:37.154 --> 03:38.823
in the last two years, separated by team.

38
03:38.906 --> 03:40.407
Is this everything?

39
03:41.158 --> 03:43.661
It's all here, as you asked.

40
03:43.744 --> 03:47.081
We will penalize you if we find anything missing.

41
03:47.164 --> 03:49.291
I'm sure you will. I know that.

42
03:49.792 --> 03:51.126
I hope that never happens.

43
03:59.051 --> 04:00.678
AUDIT IN PROGRESS AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

44
04:13.691 --> 04:15.651
Do we have to go through all that?

45
04:23.075 --> 04:25.160
- Hi, Ji-hye. - Enjoy your meal.

46
04:25.244 --> 04:26.912
- Enjoy. - You too.

47
04:27.538 --> 04:29.957
Do you think Mr. Gong and Ms. Jang ate lunch?

48
04:31.000 --> 04:34.420
They'll eat something way nicer. Why would you worry?

49
04:35.296 --> 04:36.297
Mr. Yang.

50
04:36.839 --> 04:38.090
What will happen to Division 2?

51
04:38.465 --> 04:40.426
All we have so far is a tip-off.

52
04:40.885 --> 04:42.177
They might find nothing.

53
04:42.553 --> 04:44.471
I don't know much about this

54
04:45.222 --> 04:47.224
but I hope they don't find anything.

55
04:47.808 --> 04:49.894
Do you think that's the best outcome?

56
04:49.977 --> 04:50.978
Of course.

57
04:51.061 --> 04:55.608
We're all family here. I hope no one has to suffer.

58
04:56.358 --> 04:57.860
Why would no one suffer?

59
04:58.319 --> 05:01.280
If they find nothing, Mr. Gong and Ms. Jang suffer.

60
05:02.114 --> 05:04.700
Oh, is that how it works?

61
05:04.783 --> 05:07.620
When it's about work, there's no such thing as nothing.

62
05:07.703 --> 05:09.330
There must always be a result.

63
05:09.788 --> 05:12.958
The only difference is whether it's a scratch or a grave injury.

64
05:14.335 --> 05:18.589
Then we should hope they find something.

65
05:19.006 --> 05:20.424
My personal wish is

66
05:21.300 --> 05:23.552
that they find a small mistake that results in a scratch.

67
05:24.178 --> 05:26.805
Best-case scenario, everyone gets off with a scratch.

68
05:27.723 --> 05:29.850
Is there anything we could do to help?

69
05:30.559 --> 05:32.311
In that case, Ji-hye...

70
05:33.520 --> 05:36.315
Pray and hope the heavens help us.

71
05:36.398 --> 05:37.775
So they return unscathed.

72
05:38.400 --> 05:39.401
Okay.

73
05:41.779 --> 05:43.948
I love that you cut up the pork cutlet.

74
05:44.031 --> 05:46.575
Wait, you said you didn't want any.

75
05:50.162 --> 05:51.163
Mr. Lee Jong-hyun.

76
05:52.122 --> 05:54.416
You've done business with us for seven years.

77
05:54.792 --> 05:55.793
Yes.

78
05:56.085 --> 05:58.712
Considering the circumstances, I'll get to the point.

79
05:59.254 --> 06:01.340
Sure. That would benefit everyone.

80
06:04.385 --> 06:07.513
I checked the details of the contract you signed with us.

81
06:07.596 --> 06:09.682
It says the margin is 70%.

82
06:10.224 --> 06:12.685
Given the brand's recognition and influence overseas

83
06:13.143 --> 06:15.479
it's a much better offer than usual.

84
06:16.230 --> 06:18.357
Can you describe how the negotiations went?

85
06:18.941 --> 06:20.109
Hang on.

86
06:21.527 --> 06:22.820
Isn't the margin way too low?

87
06:24.154 --> 06:27.783
It is. It's almost the same as what we get.

88
06:27.866 --> 06:30.536
Division 1 imports foreign brands

89
06:30.828 --> 06:32.663
and Division 2 exports domestic brands

90
06:32.746 --> 06:34.707
and yet the margin is almost the same?

91
06:35.457 --> 06:37.793
Domestic brands aren't that well-known overseas.

92
06:37.876 --> 06:40.004
Shouldn't Division 2 get a bigger margin?

93
06:40.087 --> 06:41.797
There could be a side agreement.

94
06:42.256 --> 06:45.801
The contract says 70%, but in reality, they get 75%.

95
06:46.301 --> 06:48.929
And someone pockets the 5% difference.

96
06:54.101 --> 06:56.645
Our brand has weakened since

97
06:56.729 --> 07:00.190
but we once hit 50 billion won in sales with a single brand.

98
07:00.899 --> 07:03.444
Our brand awareness in Asia is improving.

99
07:05.571 --> 07:07.448
I don't think we're taking too much.

100
07:08.907 --> 07:10.743
Did you bring the contract?

101
07:11.201 --> 07:12.619
I believe we asked you to.

102
07:17.916 --> 07:18.959
Here you go.

103
07:19.960 --> 07:21.628
He won't admit to it.

104
07:21.712 --> 07:24.465
Their contract will say the same as ours.

105
07:24.548 --> 07:26.717
There's no issue with the contract.

106
07:27.801 --> 07:31.430
We can't find anything unless we check their accounts.

107
07:31.930 --> 07:34.349
You won't get anything from the accounts, either.

108
07:34.725 --> 07:37.811
They made it so business expenses don't require receipts.

109
07:38.145 --> 07:39.563
They'd have paid in cash.

110
07:40.272 --> 07:42.733
How about pressuring them by saying we'll file a complaint?

111
07:45.819 --> 07:46.820
Mr. Lee.

112
07:47.404 --> 07:50.908
We suspect you paid kickbacks under the table.

113
07:52.701 --> 07:54.161
That's nonsense.

114
07:55.204 --> 07:56.580
There were no kickbacks.

115
07:57.664 --> 08:00.667
Admit to it now, and it'll be kept between us.

116
08:01.293 --> 08:05.089
We can penalize our personnel, and you can handle yours.

117
08:05.881 --> 08:07.382
However, if you don't admit to it

118
08:08.092 --> 08:09.843
we have no choice but to involve prosecution.

119
08:11.053 --> 08:13.055
Do you have any proof to warrant that?

120
08:14.139 --> 08:17.810
Would a prosecutor investigate on suspicion only, without proof?

121
08:18.060 --> 08:19.353
There's circumstantial evidence.

122
08:19.812 --> 08:22.731
Some of our staff have a conscience, and they blew a whistle.

123
08:25.109 --> 08:26.443
File a complaint and have them investigate.

124
08:28.487 --> 08:31.782
But if they don't find anything

125
08:32.366 --> 08:34.326
I will hold Hongsung responsible.

126
08:35.452 --> 08:36.453
How?

127
08:37.955 --> 08:39.623
How will you hold us responsible?

128
08:41.792 --> 08:44.211
Do you think we're incapable of taking action?

129
08:44.920 --> 08:47.923
Is that why you're saying you'll do something

130
08:48.715 --> 08:50.717
when you can't really do anything?

131
08:51.927 --> 08:54.054
You've gone a little too far.

132
08:54.888 --> 08:57.015
Is this the price I pay for doing business with Hongsung?

133
08:57.599 --> 08:59.977
You can't treat me like a common criminal.

134
09:01.103 --> 09:05.399
They wouldn't have come this far if a warning worked at all.

135
09:05.816 --> 09:08.986
True. They'd be well-prepared.

136
09:09.319 --> 09:11.029
This is as far as an audit can go.

137
09:11.530 --> 09:15.242
We can't check personal accounts or search another company's office.

138
09:17.411 --> 09:18.787
I really hate it

139
09:19.621 --> 09:20.747
but in this situation

140
09:21.081 --> 09:23.292
the only thing we can do is give a warning.

141
09:23.750 --> 09:26.503
"We know what you did, but we'll let you off this time."

142
09:27.171 --> 09:29.214
That alone works sometimes.

143
09:29.548 --> 09:31.175
Most people decide to play it safe.

144
09:32.843 --> 09:34.678
We can't do that this time.

145
09:34.761 --> 09:38.182
The VP ordered this audit, and the whole board is involved.

146
09:39.308 --> 09:41.351
We must bring them something.

147
09:42.019 --> 09:43.645
Then find me something.

148
09:44.021 --> 09:46.231
All I know is the law, and it looks fine to me.

149
09:50.611 --> 09:51.862
This is definitely odd.

150
09:54.031 --> 09:55.449
My experience tells me to focus

151
09:55.741 --> 09:57.659
on money going out rather than money coming in.

152
09:58.785 --> 10:00.287
SHIPPING COST BRICLOGIX

153
10:06.710 --> 10:09.463
Can I ask why Hongsung covered the shipping costs?

154
10:12.883 --> 10:15.177
That depends on the agreement.

155
10:15.594 --> 10:16.595
No.

156
10:17.137 --> 10:21.558
Shipping costs are never covered by the brand controller.

157
10:22.017 --> 10:23.602
That's included in the margin.

158
10:23.685 --> 10:25.520
That might never happen elsewhere

159
10:26.104 --> 10:27.189
but we agreed to it.

160
10:27.814 --> 10:29.775
That's how considerate Mr. Choi is.

161
10:30.525 --> 10:32.444
Ask him about it.

162
10:32.527 --> 10:33.654
We already did.

163
10:37.032 --> 10:38.700
That's the shipping company's bank statement.

164
10:39.534 --> 10:41.995
It's a sole proprietorship, so it conducts transactions freely.

165
10:42.746 --> 10:44.122
The owner already confessed

166
10:44.748 --> 10:47.376
to receiving payments from both companies

167
10:47.668 --> 10:50.170
laundering them as salaries, and returning the money to you.

168
10:53.131 --> 10:54.800
This is what I think happened.

169
10:55.968 --> 10:57.511
You kept getting off with warnings

170
10:57.594 --> 10:59.263
and no one actually did anything.

171
10:59.721 --> 11:01.056
So you got more brazen.

172
11:03.058 --> 11:04.101
You and us both.

173
11:09.606 --> 11:11.358
Will you admit to it now?

174
11:18.365 --> 11:19.366
Jeez.

175
11:21.159 --> 11:23.245
You should've said from the start that you knew everything.

176
11:24.705 --> 11:26.665
Why did you make me lie?

177
11:28.709 --> 11:29.710
We gave you a chance.

178
11:31.336 --> 11:32.963
And you just lost it.

179
11:43.390 --> 11:46.310
You should've said it was a fucking chance.

180
12:01.867 --> 12:03.410
How much is the shipping cost?

181
12:09.541 --> 12:11.960
It's 2% of the total invoiced amount.

182
12:12.336 --> 12:14.421
You took it, but instead of keeping it all to yourself

183
12:15.505 --> 12:17.174
you gave some of it to the brand?

184
12:19.509 --> 12:20.510
I'm asking you.

185
12:22.429 --> 12:23.430
I'm sorry, sir.

186
12:24.765 --> 12:27.601
He got a kickback from a kickback.

187
12:28.935 --> 12:31.063
He knew you were taking from the company

188
12:31.438 --> 12:33.857
so he asked you for a piece of the pie.

189
12:34.983 --> 12:37.611
What did they take us for, making a demand like that?

190
12:38.570 --> 12:39.571
I'm sorry, sir.

191
12:42.032 --> 12:43.200
What are you sorry about?

192
12:44.493 --> 12:46.328
You wouldn't have done this if you felt bad.

193
12:47.788 --> 12:48.789
Mr. Gong.

194
12:49.498 --> 12:50.499
Yes, sir.

195
12:51.750 --> 12:54.294
Apart from the shipping costs, you suspect a side agreement?

196
12:54.753 --> 12:57.172
Yes, the brand margin was excessively high.

197
12:57.255 --> 12:59.633
VICE PRESIDENT KOO IN-MOCK

198
13:01.843 --> 13:02.844
Mr. Choi.

199
13:04.054 --> 13:05.180
Yes, sir.

200
13:06.556 --> 13:08.308
How about you admit to what you did

201
13:09.226 --> 13:11.103
cough up as much of the money you can

202
13:12.521 --> 13:14.022
and leave voluntarily?

203
13:19.778 --> 13:21.196
Do you need time to think?

204
13:22.406 --> 13:24.116
No, sir.

205
13:26.576 --> 13:29.538
I'll cooperate with the Audit Team.

206
13:33.083 --> 13:34.918
- Yoon. - Yes, sir.

207
13:35.794 --> 13:37.754
Aren't you the youngest associate director?

208
13:38.296 --> 13:39.673
Yes, I am.

209
13:40.257 --> 13:42.217
You might also have the shortest tenure ever.

210
13:45.178 --> 13:46.680
This is why

211
13:47.097 --> 13:49.099
you should never be proud of an early promotion

212
13:49.182 --> 13:51.977
or despair that things are taking too long for you.

213
13:52.853 --> 13:54.438
This is what people are like.

214
13:55.772 --> 13:58.191
Some rise fast only to fall fast.

215
13:59.609 --> 14:02.737
I have nothing more to say about that.

216
14:08.618 --> 14:09.619
Ms. Park.

217
14:10.203 --> 14:11.204
Yes, sir.

218
14:11.621 --> 14:13.832
Handle Division 2 as well for a while.

219
14:17.627 --> 14:18.628
Any issues with that?

220
14:19.379 --> 14:20.380
No, sir.

221
14:59.127 --> 15:00.212
You can go ahead.

222
15:11.848 --> 15:13.183
HOT MILK COFFEE 600 WON

223
15:20.899 --> 15:21.900
Thank you.

224
15:28.198 --> 15:29.533
I haven't been here in a while.

225
15:30.158 --> 15:31.826
We used to sit out here often.

226
15:32.827 --> 15:36.248
Our presence makes other employees uncomfortable.

227
15:37.832 --> 15:39.209
Exactly.

228
15:39.834 --> 15:42.754
Is it the title or the age?

229
15:42.837 --> 15:44.756
Everyone complains about us.

230
15:47.926 --> 15:49.177
What will you do next?

231
15:51.304 --> 15:52.389
I don't know.

232
15:53.014 --> 15:55.141
I'm too afraid to do my own thing

233
15:56.017 --> 15:57.978
so I'd like to find a decent opening.

234
15:58.478 --> 16:01.982
But I doubt anyone would want a troublemaker like me.

235
16:02.983 --> 16:04.484
It's too late for regret.

236
16:05.944 --> 16:07.195
Sorry about that.

237
16:09.281 --> 16:10.365
I get it, though.

238
16:11.283 --> 16:13.451
I think I might have done the same.

239
16:15.036 --> 16:17.914
A uselessly lofty title means more expenses.

240
16:18.331 --> 16:21.001
People are watching, so you have to be seen at decent places

241
16:21.543 --> 16:23.670
but not places that are too fancy.

242
16:24.963 --> 16:28.174
Others with our titles own a nice place and a nice car

243
16:29.551 --> 16:31.803
yet you're still struggling to pay off a mortgage.

244
16:32.387 --> 16:34.514
That's when you start to want more.

245
16:35.849 --> 16:38.435
It doesn't help that others embezzle too.

246
16:39.352 --> 16:41.855
It feels like staying honest means falling behind.

247
16:42.480 --> 16:46.818
It starts off by accepting a kickback you're offered.

248
16:47.193 --> 16:49.654
Then you end up stealing the shipping costs.

249
16:52.240 --> 16:54.659
It doesn't take much to become lousy.

250
16:55.410 --> 16:57.912
Even people like you, who were once so decent.

251
16:59.039 --> 17:00.624
I have no excuses.

252
17:01.958 --> 17:03.126
Don't say that.

253
17:03.835 --> 17:06.463
I didn't bring you out here to lecture you.

254
17:06.546 --> 17:09.591
No, I should've been...

255
17:10.675 --> 17:12.636
I should've been lectured.

256
17:13.803 --> 17:16.181
If I'd remained under you...

257
17:19.934 --> 17:21.436
this wouldn't have happened.

258
17:24.731 --> 17:27.359
Being a parent whose child committed a crime.

259
17:28.276 --> 17:29.527
Do you know that feeling?

260
17:30.737 --> 17:32.864
The child must pay for what they did.

261
17:35.492 --> 17:37.035
But despite what they did

262
17:38.578 --> 17:41.289
you still love your child.

263
17:44.125 --> 17:46.586
You wonder if you failed them somehow.

264
17:48.922 --> 17:51.132
- That's it. - I'm so sorry.

265
17:53.802 --> 17:54.803
I just...

266
17:56.388 --> 17:57.472
I just wanted to have

267
17:58.431 --> 18:00.892
a coffee out here with you like the old times.

268
18:04.729 --> 18:06.481
Tell me when you decide what to do.

269
18:07.524 --> 18:08.983
And if you need help.

270
18:09.567 --> 18:10.568
I will.

271
18:12.237 --> 18:13.571
Thank you, Ms. Park.

272
18:14.656 --> 18:15.740
Thank you.

273
18:26.835 --> 18:28.628
- Mr. Gong. - Yes?

274
18:29.587 --> 18:31.631
How did it go? I haven't heard anything.

275
18:33.383 --> 18:35.260
The Audit Team will be wrapping it up.

276
18:39.806 --> 18:41.141
Did you see the holiday gift?

277
18:45.145 --> 18:47.564
But they left her out again...

278
18:48.314 --> 18:49.566
Sorry to interrupt, Mr. Gong.

279
18:50.066 --> 18:51.568
No, go ahead.

280
18:52.610 --> 18:53.945
Did you check my proposal?

281
18:54.612 --> 18:55.613
Yes, I did.

282
18:56.406 --> 18:59.159
The son of the mall's VP is getting married this weekend?

283
18:59.242 --> 19:01.578
Yes, we sent a flower arrangement in Hongsung's name.

284
19:02.036 --> 19:03.371
Who paid for it?

285
19:04.164 --> 19:06.708
We put it on your card.

286
19:06.791 --> 19:09.043
You should've put it on the director's card.

287
19:09.127 --> 19:11.963
She told us to put it on yours.

288
19:12.046 --> 19:13.339
Darn it.

289
19:15.508 --> 19:16.968
What is it this time?

290
19:20.722 --> 19:23.683
There's something we must sort out before the holiday.

291
19:25.268 --> 19:26.394
Let's do it now.

292
19:32.233 --> 19:34.944
- What is this? - An idea Team 4 came up with.

293
19:35.820 --> 19:36.821
Team 4?

294
19:38.072 --> 19:39.407
How are things over there?

295
19:40.658 --> 19:44.621
Mr. Oh is struggling with the workload without a superior.

296
19:46.247 --> 19:47.874
Let's do it one at a time.

297
19:47.957 --> 19:49.459
Don't you see the mess I'm in?

298
19:49.542 --> 19:52.796
I'm figuring out Division 2 on top of my usual workload.

299
19:59.010 --> 20:00.553
They want to work for a commission?

300
20:01.179 --> 20:03.264
The profit is low, but so is the risk.

301
20:03.348 --> 20:05.850
I thought it could be a decent long-term project.

302
20:06.976 --> 20:09.145
- Mr. Oh brought this to you? - Yes.

303
20:10.688 --> 20:11.731
Was it his idea?

304
20:12.732 --> 20:14.526
I'm not sure about that.

305
20:15.193 --> 20:16.444
Get him in here.

306
20:19.948 --> 20:21.908
Come and sit next to him.

307
20:21.991 --> 20:23.159
- Hello, sir. - Hi.

308
20:26.704 --> 20:29.624
Did you come up with this on your own?

309
20:30.542 --> 20:33.711
It was Mr. Jeong's idea, but I came up with all the details.

310
20:33.795 --> 20:35.797
He said it would be a good first project.

311
20:37.882 --> 20:41.928
I can tell how much you've put into your first project.

312
20:42.720 --> 20:43.888
It's like my own baby.

313
20:45.974 --> 20:47.100
Oh, dear...

314
20:48.601 --> 20:51.521
Jeong was way worse than I thought.

315
20:57.277 --> 21:00.905
A non-profit business isn't just for anyone.

316
21:01.781 --> 21:03.992
First, we must survive until we turn a profit.

317
21:04.993 --> 21:06.327
Even when the industry is booming

318
21:06.411 --> 21:09.247
no one would rely on a single non-profit business.

319
21:10.540 --> 21:12.667
See if they're doing business with Jeong's company.

320
21:13.376 --> 21:16.421
I bet they signed the real business with a huge margin.

321
21:17.088 --> 21:20.508
We do all the hard work while Jeong takes all the profit.

322
21:22.385 --> 21:23.970
Do you get what I'm saying, Mr. Oh?

323
21:25.138 --> 21:26.139
Yes.

324
21:29.058 --> 21:31.060
You made a decent dish, but the ingredients were rotten.

325
21:31.519 --> 21:33.062
Bring me something else.

326
21:33.605 --> 21:35.732
I liked the details, so don't blame yourself.

327
21:36.691 --> 21:38.568
Yes, sir. Thank you.

328
21:39.110 --> 21:41.362
You can go. Gong, you stay.

329
21:55.084 --> 21:57.211
Do you know how humiliating that is?

330
21:58.379 --> 22:01.633
If we approve this after demolishing a whole division

331
22:01.883 --> 22:03.927
they'll call us honest but incompetent.

332
22:05.595 --> 22:08.806
Do you want them to say they'd rather hire

333
22:08.890 --> 22:10.183
a competent but dishonest man?

334
22:15.063 --> 22:16.439
Eun-tae.

335
22:16.773 --> 22:19.108
You really worry me sometimes.

336
22:21.361 --> 22:24.280
Have you ever driven a nice car?

337
22:25.907 --> 22:28.868
- Pardon? - You know, an expensive, fast car.

338
22:30.286 --> 22:32.872
I once got to sit in the passenger seat.

339
22:33.706 --> 22:35.875
Didn't you feel uneasy?

340
22:37.752 --> 22:40.254
When a bad driver handles a fancy car

341
22:40.838 --> 22:42.882
it's the passenger who suffers.

342
22:46.886 --> 22:48.388
Your car is way too fancy.

343
22:49.013 --> 22:50.181
Watch how you drive it.

344
23:47.280 --> 23:49.115
- I don't think it looks right. - Really?

345
23:49.907 --> 23:52.577
The brighter color might work since it's women's wear.

346
23:54.037 --> 23:55.413
Yes, but the current trend...

347
23:55.747 --> 23:56.873
But still...

348
23:57.540 --> 23:59.083
What about the other colors?

349
23:59.500 --> 24:01.836
- Something brighter. - Brighter?

350
24:02.253 --> 24:04.338
- Isn't this too bright? - Are you all staying late?

351
24:05.048 --> 24:07.675
We have some stuff to wrap up.

352
24:08.092 --> 24:09.302
It must be done before the holiday.

353
24:09.802 --> 24:11.262
Finish it up and go home.

354
24:11.888 --> 24:12.930
I'm heading out.

355
24:13.931 --> 24:15.099
Bye, Mr. Gong.

356
24:15.433 --> 24:17.351
- Goodbye. - Enjoy the holiday break.

357
24:32.450 --> 24:33.451
Mr. Gong!

358
24:37.955 --> 24:39.582
You left this behind.

359
24:43.377 --> 24:46.214
I gave it to you. Take it home.

360
24:47.673 --> 24:50.093
No, sir. It's fine.

361
24:51.344 --> 24:52.720
I want you to have it.

362
24:55.431 --> 24:56.432
Mr. Gong.

363
24:58.142 --> 24:59.644
You don't have to do this.

364
25:00.311 --> 25:01.979
Please, just take the gift.

365
25:03.648 --> 25:04.690
Okay, then.

366
25:10.488 --> 25:14.158
I'm really grateful, but...

367
25:15.243 --> 25:18.621
When Gi-tae made that mistake, his first concern was

368
25:19.372 --> 25:23.459
if it would cost me a full-time position.

369
25:24.377 --> 25:27.338
No one cares if a contract worker gets a holiday gift or not

370
25:27.964 --> 25:30.550
but you left this under my desk.

371
25:31.884 --> 25:34.137
I'm really grateful, but...

372
25:39.475 --> 25:41.227
The more you care...

373
25:45.189 --> 25:46.691
the more I feel like a contract worker.

374
25:51.737 --> 25:53.781
I should get back to work now.

375
25:55.908 --> 25:57.326
Enjoy your holiday.

376
26:07.503 --> 26:08.546
It was a mistake.

377
26:10.506 --> 26:14.051
A mistake I can't make up, no matter how hard I try.

378
26:21.726 --> 26:23.978
Today, I ruined a few colleagues' livelihoods.

379
26:27.190 --> 26:29.400
They might have done wrong

380
26:30.735 --> 26:33.654
but I was the one to reveal it and get them punished.

381
26:38.451 --> 26:40.620
My superior criticized me.

382
26:41.954 --> 26:44.790
The one thing an employee must never hear.

383
26:46.542 --> 26:48.753
"It's better to be corrupt than incompetent."

384
26:49.420 --> 26:50.546
That's what he said to me.

385
26:50.630 --> 26:52.048
VERNIA STUDIO GLOBAL EXPANSION BUSINESS PLAN

386
27:07.688 --> 27:10.733
I offended a team member in the name of consideration.

387
27:15.488 --> 27:17.782
I didn't give her the gift for her sake.

388
27:18.658 --> 27:20.409
I did it for my own.

389
27:23.663 --> 27:25.706
- That was so good. - I really enjoyed that.

390
27:25.790 --> 27:27.166
It's a famous place.

391
27:27.250 --> 27:29.210
It was incredible. Seriously.

392
27:29.293 --> 27:30.753
Down for another round?

393
27:30.836 --> 27:31.963
- Let's go somewhere. - For real?

394
27:32.046 --> 27:33.589
- What should we eat? - What do you want?

395
28:07.081 --> 28:08.124
Today

396
28:08.624 --> 28:12.837
as a colleague, a subordinate, and a superior

397
28:13.462 --> 28:14.880
I accomplished nothing.

398
28:18.092 --> 28:19.969
I thought things were going well.

399
28:20.803 --> 28:24.598
I'm rich, so I no longer work to earn a living.

400
28:25.016 --> 28:28.894
I don't work for the money, so the work became clearer.

401
28:30.646 --> 28:32.606
I thought everything had changed.

402
28:33.316 --> 28:35.026
(I can't believe what I'm hearing.)

403
28:35.901 --> 28:37.778
My circumstances might have improved.

404
28:39.238 --> 28:42.116
But in reality, nothing has changed.

405
28:49.040 --> 28:50.166
I was still

406
28:51.250 --> 28:52.752
a nobody.

407
29:17.485 --> 29:18.986
I JUST ARRIVED IN BUSAN, MOM

408
29:19.070 --> 29:20.446
I'M MEETING SOMEONE FIRST SEE YOU LATER

409
29:24.575 --> 29:26.786
THE X-COORDINATE OF A EQUALS ALPHA...

410
29:46.847 --> 29:48.974
Multiply both sides by 4x.

411
29:49.058 --> 29:51.102
Uncle, when did you get here?

412
29:51.727 --> 29:52.728
A long time ago.

413
29:53.062 --> 29:54.563
You're joking.

414
29:54.647 --> 29:55.898
I was watching to see when you'd come.

415
29:56.357 --> 29:58.734
You're studying here when you don't even study at school?

416
29:58.818 --> 30:01.695
I study whenever and wherever I can.

417
30:01.779 --> 30:04.448
- You just don't know me. - You and your nonsense.

418
30:05.157 --> 30:07.785
- Wait up. - Should we eat something?

419
30:07.868 --> 30:09.787
Will you buy me what I want?

420
30:09.870 --> 30:11.622
Name it first. I'll think about it.

421
30:12.206 --> 30:13.582
I want something expensive.

422
30:16.293 --> 30:18.546
You said you'd buy me what I wanted.

423
30:18.629 --> 30:19.880
I didn't say that.

424
30:20.297 --> 30:21.715
Then why did you even ask?

425
30:21.799 --> 30:23.175
To eat anything but that.

426
30:24.051 --> 30:25.970
Jeez, I should order some soju.

427
30:26.053 --> 30:27.179
Do you want a shot?

428
30:27.930 --> 30:29.557
You're a horrible uncle.

429
30:29.640 --> 30:31.142
I used to drink at your age.

430
30:31.809 --> 30:33.686
These days, only delinquents drink at my age.

431
30:33.769 --> 30:36.230
I'm only half a delinquent, so I can't drink.

432
30:37.064 --> 30:39.316
Eat up. Food in Seoul isn't that special, either.

433
30:39.400 --> 30:41.193
Who eats this these days?

434
30:41.861 --> 30:44.113
I wanted something from a famous chain.

435
30:47.908 --> 30:49.076
What's this?

436
30:52.913 --> 30:54.248
Isn't this a luxury brand?

437
30:54.331 --> 30:56.333
- You know it? - Of course, I do.

438
30:56.750 --> 30:58.502
The celebs carry this stuff.

439
30:58.586 --> 31:00.629
I heard teenagers like it too.

440
31:01.422 --> 31:02.423
Is it for me?

441
31:05.426 --> 31:08.846
Uncle, is this how much you care about me?

442
31:09.138 --> 31:11.474
The food will taste much better now, won't it?

443
31:11.849 --> 31:12.850
Yeah.

444
31:19.565 --> 31:21.442
You can't post about it, okay?

445
31:21.859 --> 31:24.278
I won't. It'll get stolen if I take it to school.

446
31:25.196 --> 31:27.406
Do you get beaten up and stuff?

447
31:28.073 --> 31:29.283
I don't.

448
31:29.658 --> 31:31.952
You need to tell me right away if you do.

449
31:32.036 --> 31:33.996
I hope you don't get beaten up yourself.

450
31:36.832 --> 31:37.833
The bus is here.

451
31:38.626 --> 31:39.919
I'll go ahead.

452
31:40.002 --> 31:42.254
Get a coffee somewhere and take your time.

453
31:42.338 --> 31:43.339
What?

454
31:43.422 --> 31:45.591
You told me to meet you so you could stay out late.

455
31:46.300 --> 31:48.886
- Well... - Try living with my dad.

456
31:48.969 --> 31:50.179
You grow up really quickly.

457
31:50.763 --> 31:52.056
Come home before dinner.

458
32:53.701 --> 32:55.452
DONGRAE ALTERATIONS

459
33:11.760 --> 33:12.761
You're here.

460
33:14.013 --> 33:15.431
Yes, I'm here, Dad.

461
33:15.806 --> 33:16.807
THE NEW TESTAMENT

462
33:17.558 --> 33:19.518
Go upstairs. Your mom's waiting for you.

463
33:20.019 --> 33:21.020
Okay.

464
33:22.062 --> 33:23.063
Wait.

465
33:23.772 --> 33:25.608
Your belt buckle's a little loose.

466
33:26.317 --> 33:27.526
Give it to me.

467
33:29.069 --> 33:30.404
It looks fine to me.

468
33:30.487 --> 33:31.989
It's not. Hand it over.

469
33:43.626 --> 33:44.627
Go up now.

470
33:45.294 --> 33:47.546
Okay, see you there.

471
34:00.809 --> 34:02.519
You prepare way too much food.

472
34:02.603 --> 34:04.313
- We'll never... - I'll pack some for Eun-tae.

473
34:04.396 --> 34:06.857
We should have plenty for Eun-seok too.

474
34:06.940 --> 34:09.485
It's too much food, even for that.

475
34:09.568 --> 34:11.445
Mom, I'm home.

476
34:11.528 --> 34:13.947
Oh, my gosh. Eun-tae's home.

477
34:14.031 --> 34:16.116
- Hello, Eun-tae. - How are you?

478
34:16.200 --> 34:18.535
You should've come home earlier.

479
34:18.619 --> 34:20.371
My dear boy...

480
34:20.954 --> 34:22.373
- You look dreadful. - What?

481
34:22.456 --> 34:24.375
Have you been starving yourself?

482
34:24.750 --> 34:27.169
I told you to eat on time.

483
34:27.252 --> 34:29.463
Do you still eat junk food all the time?

484
34:29.546 --> 34:31.799
Oh, enough with the nagging, Mother.

485
34:31.882 --> 34:33.634
Give him time to breathe.

486
34:34.134 --> 34:36.762
Leave it. Berating me gives her joy.

487
34:38.097 --> 34:39.640
Hello, Uncle.

488
34:39.723 --> 34:41.392
Long time no see, A-yeong.

489
34:41.475 --> 34:43.352
You made the long trip to Busan.

490
34:44.728 --> 34:46.021
Too bad, though.

491
34:46.105 --> 34:48.023
- The delay was for nothing. - What?

492
34:48.315 --> 34:49.525
Are you here, Eun-tae?

493
34:54.446 --> 34:55.823
Why did you come so late?

494
34:56.407 --> 34:57.783
Didn't you go to work?

495
34:57.866 --> 35:01.245
No, I heard you'd visit, so I swapped shifts.

496
35:01.495 --> 35:02.955
Go wash your hands. Let's eat.

497
35:03.038 --> 35:04.873
Anything good for dinner, Mom?

498
35:05.207 --> 35:06.250
Let's see.

499
35:06.333 --> 35:07.584
Oh, you made skewers.

500
35:07.668 --> 35:09.002
Gosh, it's hot.

501
35:09.795 --> 35:11.630
You didn't even wash your hands.

502
35:12.589 --> 35:15.426
So how are things at work?

503
35:18.178 --> 35:19.805
Why would you ask about work?

504
35:20.597 --> 35:23.559
Why not? Can't I ask my little brother about his job?

505
35:24.351 --> 35:27.646
I know you don't care about it. Get to the point.

506
35:29.857 --> 35:33.152
Can you promise me one thing first?

507
35:34.069 --> 35:37.489
Don't get annoyed and hear me out first.

508
35:38.699 --> 35:41.243
Why should I have to promise that? Just talk.

509
35:47.124 --> 35:48.167
Take a look at this.

510
35:51.420 --> 35:56.300
It's a door hinge that prevents people from getting hurt.

511
35:56.675 --> 35:58.969
There's a huge demand for it.

512
35:59.052 --> 36:02.014
It's going into almost every new apartment.

513
36:02.556 --> 36:05.851
A surprising number of people get hurt in door hinges.

514
36:07.060 --> 36:08.145
It looks pretty good.

515
36:09.313 --> 36:11.023
There's this guy who makes these.

516
36:11.690 --> 36:14.318
The deals are secured

517
36:14.401 --> 36:18.155
but he doesn't have the money to keep the factory going.

518
36:18.697 --> 36:21.992
He says he needs about 100 million won.

519
36:23.327 --> 36:24.536
I plan to invest.

520
36:25.829 --> 36:27.039
With what money?

521
36:27.456 --> 36:29.708
That's why I'm talking to you.

522
36:33.295 --> 36:34.296
Could you

523
36:35.923 --> 36:38.425
get me 100 million won?

524
36:43.055 --> 36:44.056
Eun-seok.

525
36:46.600 --> 36:50.020
You said some guy made that already.

526
36:50.771 --> 36:52.856
If he signed deals, there would be sales.

527
36:53.190 --> 36:56.735
A bank would loan him the money if he had signed contracts.

528
36:56.819 --> 37:00.531
Getting a loan is like broadcasting he doesn't have the money.

529
37:01.406 --> 37:03.951
I've known him since I started my own businesses.

530
37:04.618 --> 37:07.454
He can be trusted, okay?

531
37:08.330 --> 37:09.790
Even so.

532
37:10.374 --> 37:13.293
- That's a lot of money. - I know that

533
37:13.377 --> 37:16.380
you don't have 100 million in cash right now.

534
37:19.091 --> 37:20.092
Don't you think

535
37:21.051 --> 37:24.388
you could get a loan somehow?

536
37:29.977 --> 37:31.603
You want me to take out a loan?

537
37:32.604 --> 37:33.605
Eun-tae.

538
37:34.439 --> 37:36.733
I know I got myself into a lot of trouble so far.

539
37:36.817 --> 37:39.611
- How can you say that? - Hear me out, will you?

540
37:39.903 --> 37:42.531
- I have a hunch. - Will you stop it?

541
37:46.618 --> 37:47.786
It's a holiday.

542
37:48.996 --> 37:50.247
Do you know I stayed out late

543
37:51.123 --> 37:52.541
just so I could avoid coming home to you?

544
37:54.793 --> 37:57.087
I did that because I knew you'd be ashamed to see me.

545
37:59.756 --> 38:03.093
But the first thing you do is ask me for money?

546
38:04.011 --> 38:05.095
Come on.

547
38:06.013 --> 38:07.347
How can you do this to me?

548
38:09.766 --> 38:10.767
Please.

549
38:12.227 --> 38:13.437
Will you grow up?

550
38:14.855 --> 38:16.189
I beg of you.

551
38:23.488 --> 38:25.365
Did you really come late to avoid me?

552
38:32.247 --> 38:33.332
I didn't know that.

553
38:35.500 --> 38:36.543
It's just that...

554
38:38.921 --> 38:40.839
I really thought this was a good idea.

555
38:45.052 --> 38:46.094
Sorry, man.

556
38:47.387 --> 38:48.847
Pretend I didn't say a thing.

557
38:53.644 --> 38:54.853
I'm going downstairs.

558
38:56.521 --> 38:57.522
Take your time.

559
40:53.263 --> 40:58.185
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

560
41:15.285 --> 41:17.037
ROOF TILE PRAYERS 10,000 PER TILE

561
41:23.668 --> 41:24.878
My dear son...

562
41:24.961 --> 41:27.380
MY DEAR SON

563
41:28.799 --> 41:30.467
May he grow up to be

564
41:31.802 --> 41:34.805
a decent human being.

565
41:34.888 --> 41:36.848
GROW UP TO BE A DECENT HUMAN BEING

566
41:40.185 --> 41:41.853
My dear Eun-tae...

567
41:43.146 --> 41:45.565
May he meet a good life partner...

568
41:45.649 --> 41:48.193
MAY HE MEET A GOOD LIFE PARTNER

569
41:48.276 --> 41:52.948
...and get married one day.

570
43:12.444 --> 43:14.321
Excuse me, Venerable Sir.

571
43:14.946 --> 43:17.407
I took a break to stretch and relax.

572
43:18.158 --> 43:22.162
Does that mean I have to start over?

573
43:22.954 --> 43:24.497
You can keep going.

574
43:25.123 --> 43:26.249
Okay, thank you.

575
43:36.218 --> 43:38.345
MY DEAR SON... MY DEAR EUN-TAE...

576
43:39.971 --> 43:41.973
MY DEAR SEON-HYUK...

577
43:44.100 --> 43:46.353
MAY HIS BUSINESS FLOURISH ONE WAY OR ANOTHER

578
46:20.006 --> 46:21.966
Subtitles by Jennifer Jean Lim
